  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for freeipmi",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for freeipmi fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-85504: stack-based buffer overflow via malformed Fujitsu SEL long-text responses (bsc#1278719).\n- CVE-2026-85505: Denial of Service via stack-based buffer over-read in ipmi-oem (bsc#1278722).\n- CVE-2026-85506: Arbitrary code execution via stack-based buffer overflow in ipmi-oem (bsc#1278721).\n- CVE-2026-85507: stack-based buffer overflow in _output_dell_system_info_cmc_info (bsc#1278724).\n- CVE-2026-85508: stack-based buffer overflow in _output_dell_system_info_cmc_ipv6_info (bsc#1278726).\n- CVE-2026-85509: stack-based buffer overflow when a BMC returns more bytes than requested (bsc#1278727).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
